; Output: PCM86.M
; Console: PCM86.OUT
; PMDMML.MAN §13-2, §5-2, §4-4

#Title PCM86
#Option /v/c

; The PCM86 part. The voice table and the sample data are not part of the
; module: they come from the .P86 file the PMD trace tests load, the way
; P86DRV does. The notes select the two voices, and move the pan and volume
; registers the PCM86 driver writes; o7 makes the /S octave shift visible.
; The 96th-note lengths keep each note to one Timer B tick.
J @0 V255 px+64 o4 c96
J @1 V0 px-100 o7 e96
J @0 V128 px0,1 o5 d96
